{"id":"71c5426cce937ee1","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-df-projective-curve.md","title":"Projective Curve","display":"df-projective-curve — Projective Curve","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-projective-curve","aliases":["58-df-projective-curve","Projective Curve"],"display":"df-projective-curve — Projective Curve","depends_on":["[[58-df-projective-variety]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-projective-curve"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-projective-curve</span><span>Projective Curve</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-projective-curve — Projective Curve"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"6046552157f71d9c\" href=\"?note=6046552157f71d9c\" title=\"58-df-projective-variety\">58-df-projective-variety</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\">\\(k\\)</span> (algebraically closed field)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"C\\subseteq P\">\\(C\\subseteq P\\)</span> (projective-variety carrier in ambient projective space <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"P\">\\(P\\)</span> over <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\">\\(k\\)</span>, with dimension parameter <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span> and Zariski topology <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau_Z\">\\(\\tau_Z\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ProjectiveVariety}_S(C;P,k,n,\\tau_Z)\">\\(\\operatorname{ProjectiveVariety}_S(C;P,k,n,\\tau_Z)\\)</span> (exact irreducible projective-variety predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"6046552157f71d9c\" href=\"?note=6046552157f71d9c\" title=\"58-df-projective-variety\">58-df-projective-variety</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{KrullDimensionOne}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{KrullDimensionOne}_S\\)</span> (topological predicates defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ProjectiveCurve}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ProjectiveCurve}_S\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}projective\\text{-}curve\\text{-}irreducible\\text{-}closed}\\vdash \\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S(F,C,\\tau_Z)\\leftrightarrow\\varnothing\\neq F\\subseteq C\\land\\exists U\\in\\tau_Z\\;(C\\setminus F=U\\cap C)\\land\\forall F_0,F_1\\subseteq F\\;\\left(\\left[\\exists U_0,U_1\\in\\tau_Z\\;(F\\setminus F_0=U_0\\cap F\\land F\\setminus F_1=U_1\\cap F)\\land F=F_0\\cup F_1\\right]\\to F=F_0\\lor F=F_1\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}projective\\text{-}curve\\text{-}irreducible\\text{-}closed}\\vdash \\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S(F,C,\\tau_Z)\\leftrightarrow\\varnothing\\neq F\\subseteq C\\land\\exists U\\in\\tau_Z\\;(C\\setminus F=U\\cap C)\\land\\forall F_0,F_1\\subseteq F\\;\\left(\\left[\\exists U_0,U_1\\in\\tau_Z\\;(F\\setminus F_0=U_0\\cap F\\land F\\setminus F_1=U_1\\cap F)\\land F=F_0\\cup F_1\\right]\\to F=F_0\\lor F=F_1\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}projective\\text{-}curve\\text{-}dimension\\text{-}one}\\vdash \\mathrm{KrullDimensionOne}_S(C,\\tau_Z)\\leftrightarrow\\exists F_0,F_1\\;\\left(\\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S(F_0,C,\\tau_Z)\\land\\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S(F_1,C,\\tau_Z)\\land F_0\\subsetneq F_1\\right)\\land\\neg\\exists F_0,F_1,F_2\\;\\left(\\bigwedge_{i&lt;3}\\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S(F_i,C,\\tau_Z)\\land F_0\\subsetneq F_1\\subsetneq F_2\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}projective\\text{-}curve\\text{-}dimension\\text{-}one}\\vdash \\mathrm{KrullDimensionOne}_S(C,\\tau_Z)\\leftrightarrow\\exists F_0,F_1\\;\\left(\\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S(F_0,C,\\tau_Z)\\land\\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S(F_1,C,\\tau_Z)\\land F_0\\subsetneq F_1\\right)\\land\\neg\\exists F_0,F_1,F_2\\;\\left(\\bigwedge_{i&lt;3}\\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S(F_i,C,\\tau_Z)\\land F_0\\subsetneq F_1\\subsetneq F_2\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}projective\\text{-}curve} \\vdash \\mathrm{ProjectiveCurve}_S(C,P,k,n,\\tau_Z)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{ProjectiveVariety}_S(C;P,k,n,\\tau_Z)\\land\\mathrm{KrullDimensionOne}_S(C,\\tau_Z)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}projective\\text{-}curve} \\vdash \\mathrm{ProjectiveCurve}_S(C,P,k,n,\\tau_Z)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{ProjectiveVariety}_S(C;P,k,n,\\tau_Z)\\land\\mathrm{KrullDimensionOne}_S(C,\\tau_Z)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Under the upstream convention, this atom concerns irreducible projective algebraic curves over an algebraically closed field. Scheme-theoretic integral curves over arbitrary fields require a separate scheme predicate.</li>\n<li>The ambient projective data match the upstream signature, and dimension one is expanded as the maximum length of chains of nonempty irreducible closed subsets rather than left as an unsourced <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\dim\">\\(\\dim\\)</span> operator.</li>\n<li>Genus, Riemann-Roch, and the genus formula for smooth plane curves are definitions or theorems with their own hypotheses, not clauses of this atom.</li>\n<li>Over an algebraically closed field, a smooth projective curve is a nonsingular complete one-dimensional variety.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Hartshorne, Algebraic Geometry</li>\n<li>Liu, Algebraic Geometry and Arithmetic Curves</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-projective-variety","status":"resolved","id":"6046552157f71d9c","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-projective-variety]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-projective-variety","status":"resolved","id":"6046552157f71d9c","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ProjectiveVariety}_S(C;P,k,n,\\tau_Z)$ (exact irreducible projective-variety predicate, see [[58-df-projective-variety]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"k","display":false},{"tex":"C\\subseteq P","display":false},{"tex":"P","display":false},{"tex":"k","display":false},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau_Z","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ProjectiveVariety}_S(C;P,k,n,\\tau_Z)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{KrullDimensionOne}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ProjectiveCurve}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}projective\\text{-}curve\\text{-}irreducible\\text{-}closed}\\vdash \\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S(F,C,\\tau_Z)\\leftrightarrow\\varnothing\\neq F\\subseteq C\\land\\exists U\\in\\tau_Z\\;(C\\setminus F=U\\cap C)\\land\\forall F_0,F_1\\subseteq F\\;\\left(\\left[\\exists U_0,U_1\\in\\tau_Z\\;(F\\setminus F_0=U_0\\cap F\\land F\\setminus F_1=U_1\\cap F)\\land F=F_0\\cup F_1\\right]\\to F=F_0\\lor F=F_1\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}projective\\text{-}curve\\text{-}dimension\\text{-}one}\\vdash \\mathrm{KrullDimensionOne}_S(C,\\tau_Z)\\leftrightarrow\\exists F_0,F_1\\;\\left(\\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S(F_0,C,\\tau_Z)\\land\\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S(F_1,C,\\tau_Z)\\land F_0\\subsetneq F_1\\right)\\land\\neg\\exists F_0,F_1,F_2\\;\\left(\\bigwedge_{i<3}\\mathrm{IrreducibleClosedIn}_S(F_i,C,\\tau_Z)\\land F_0\\subsetneq F_1\\subsetneq F_2\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}projective\\text{-}curve} \\vdash \\mathrm{ProjectiveCurve}_S(C,P,k,n,\\tau_Z)\\leftrightarrow\\operatorname{ProjectiveVariety}_S(C;P,k,n,\\tau_Z)\\land\\mathrm{KrullDimensionOne}_S(C,\\tau_Z)","display":true},{"tex":"\\dim","display":false}],"bytes":2645,"backlinks":[{"id":"df6e75b9887b02cd","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1001","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-projective-curve.md|58-df-projective-curve]]（batch15）"}],"outgoing":["6046552157f71d9c"]}